<title>USA: Raytheon gets $10 mln Statoil contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon gets $10 mln Statoil contract.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co said on Monday it has received a $10 million contract from Norway's Statoil to upgrade the crude oil unit at its Mongstad, Norway refinery.</p>
<p>The project includes installing a new naphtha splitter column and associated equipment that will enable the refinery to produce higher quality gasoline, the company said.</p>
<p>Raytheon will provide engineering, procurement, and construction management services for the project, which is due to be completed in October 1997.</p>
<p>Raytheon previously provided pre-engineering for the project in 1996, it said.</p>
